Equations, unknowns, systems, and constraints (@ql-equations: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @quantitative-literacy, #source @ql-source-trades-2, #source @ql-source-prealgebra, #source @ql-source-algebra, #quantitative-literacy "Functions-and-tables.lingua#r_0F4KMKK6ET8T22RG617S1RDZS2", #clean-manufacturing "../../../production/clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control/transport/A-well-mixed-volume-with-generation-and-removal.lingua#r_4CMY99W2FJ2EE3KNTFAJP15FGZ") { r_2XGYVPEJSA3GYYV0K6PYXCHXVZ
**Read:** Math for Trades, Volume 2, Working with Equations completely. Continue with Prealgebra 2e chapter 8 and Algebra and Trigonometry 2e chapter 2, then chapter 11's two- and three-variable linear systems. Work verbal, symbolic, and application exercises.

An expression can be evaluated; an equation asserts an equality that may constrain unknowns. State the allowed domain before manipulating it. Dividing by a symbol can discard the case where it is zero, and squaring can introduce a solution that fails the original equation. Substitute every proposed solution back into the original physical conditions.

For two feed streams, x + y = 100 kg/h and 0.10x + 0.30y = 20 kg/h imply x = y = 50 kg/h. The equations express total mass and component mass on the same basis. A third copy of the first equation is not a new independent constraint. Counting equations alone does not establish that a system has a unique solution.

Nonnegativity, capacity, integer counts, and specification limits restrict feasible answers. A negative mixture flow may show that a desired composition lies outside the two available feed compositions. It is a statement about feasibility, not an invitation to report a negative pipe flow without a physical interpretation.

**Work:** solve the mixture above by substitution, elimination, and a graph. Change the target component flow to 40 kg/h and explain infeasibility. Construct a pair of inconsistent equations and a pair with infinitely many solutions. Describe what extra independent observation would identify the latter. Rearrange a useful formula symbolically before inserting values so the units and singular cases remain visible.

**Continue:** [Functions, tables, domains, and inverse questions](Functions-and-tables.lingua#r_0F4KMKK6ET8T22RG617S1RDZS2).

